00:11:42.006 --> 00:11:44.252
There's Stouffer's.


00:11:44.287 --> 00:11:46.171
Should still be warm if you're hungry.


00:11:46.206 --> 00:11:48.228
WOMAN I have to tell you,
there is something magical


00:11:48.263 --> 00:11:50.250
about these rings, and
you can have it within...


00:11:50.285 --> 00:11:52.920
I wish someone would buy me a ring.


00:11:52.955 --> 00:11:55.512
Did Abby eat?


00:11:55.547 --> 00:11:56.840
What do you think?


00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:00.386
Same time tomorrow?


00:12:00.421 --> 00:12:02.012
Yep.


00:12:11.898 --> 00:12:13.482
What do we got?


00:12:13.517 --> 00:12:15.032
Okay.


00:12:15.067 --> 00:12:17.736
Well, that good-looking
guy I recognize.


00:12:17.771 --> 00:12:20.256
Who are all these other punks?


00:12:20.291 --> 00:12:22.707
My friends. It's not done yet.


00:12:22.742 --> 00:12:25.119
Well, look, you can finish
up after we eat, all right?


00:12:25.154 --> 00:12:26.492
Come get some food.


00:12:26.527 --> 00:12:27.795
I'm not hungry.


00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:30.082
Abby, please, come eat.


00:12:32.292 --> 00:12:34.586
- Come on. Here. Please come.
- No!


00:12:34.621 --> 00:12:36.171
Come and...


00:12:39.968 --> 00:12:42.512
Abs, with the day that I'm having,


00:12:42.547 --> 00:12:44.930
can you just eat some food?


00:12:45.931 --> 00:12:48.143
You're sitting on my friend.


00:12:51.021 --> 00:12:53.522
You know what? I don't care.


00:12:53.557 --> 00:12:55.357
Do whatever you want.


00:12:57.152 --> 00:12:58.820
But you should know what
happens to little kids


00:12:58.855 --> 00:13:00.196
who don't eat their dinners.


00:13:01.364 --> 00:13:04.117
Their bodies stay the same size forever.


00:13:04.152 --> 00:13:05.874
And they never get to ride


00:13:05.909 --> 00:13:08.495
the adult rides at the amusement park.


00:13:11.999 --> 00:13:14.461
My friend says you're an idiot.


00:13:14.496 --> 00:13:16.510
Mm.


00:13:16.545 --> 00:13:18.547
At least I'm real.


00:14:19.901 --> 00:14:22.653
How about some burger
with that ketchup, hon?


00:14:24.029 --> 00:14:26.156
Everything's better swimming in ketchup.


00:14:26.191 --> 00:14:29.035
Right, Mike? Whoop.


00:14:29.994 --> 00:14:31.544
I'm gonna go grab a towel.


00:14:31.579 --> 00:14:33.957
- Go watch your brother, okay?
- Okay.


00:14:35.166 --> 00:14:36.917
Garrett.


00:14:53.435 --> 00:14:54.728
Garrett?


00:15:09.743 --> 00:15:13.037
Garrett! Garrett!


00:15:37.645 --> 00:15:39.375
Just look at my nephew.


00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:41.071
It's not even 10:00


00:15:41.106 --> 00:15:43.859
and he-he can barely
keep his eyes open.


00:15:43.894 --> 00:15:46.577
And this degenerate is who they entrust


00:15:46.612 --> 00:15:48.747
with the well-being of
a mentally ill child.


00:15:48.782 --> 00:15:51.784
Jane, like I've said before,
Abby is not mentally ill.


00:15:51.819 --> 00:15:53.293
Oh, right.


00:15:53.328 --> 00:15:56.309
Perfectly normal to sit
around drawing pictures all day


00:15:56.344 --> 00:15:59.291
and-and talking to magical
creatures who do not exist.


00:15:59.326 --> 00:16:00.591
Listen, I think we all just need


00:16:00.626 --> 00:16:02.843
- to calm...
- Don't tell me to calm down.


00:16:02.878 --> 00:16:05.006
You're the doctor, and
you're making me feel like


00:16:05.041 --> 00:16:06.640
I'm the crazy one?


00:16:06.675 --> 00:16:12.638
And after... after what
he did to that poor man...


00:16:12.673 --> 00:16:13.972
I just...


00:16:20.355 --> 00:16:23.148
I have really tried
to play nice. I have.


00:16:23.183 --> 00:16:26.694
But I have to think about Abby now.


00:16:26.729 --> 00:16:28.488
Enough is enough. Doug?


00:16:29.321 --> 00:16:31.783
- Doug.
- Oh.


00:16:34.035 --> 00:16:35.751
In your heart,


00:16:35.786 --> 00:16:37.996
you know that this is
the right thing to do.


00:16:38.031 --> 00:16:39.791
I hope that you will sign.


00:16:40.624 --> 00:16:42.467
- And if I don't?
- Well, then,


00:16:42.502 --> 00:16:44.462
my lawyer and I will
have to take you to court,


00:16:44.497 --> 00:16:46.972
where any judge with an ounce of sanity


00:16:47.007 --> 00:16:51.302
will see to it that you
never see your sister again.


00:16:51.337 --> 00:16:53.310
That what you want?


00:16:53.345 --> 00:16:55.354
She-she doesn't even care about Abby.


00:16:55.389 --> 00:16:58.517
All she wants is the
monthly check from the state.


00:17:00.853 --> 00:17:02.521
But, I mean, she-she has
some good points, though.


00:17:02.556 --> 00:17:05.364
I'm hardly fit to be raising a kid.


00:17:05.399 --> 00:17:07.861
I know a little girl who
would strongly disagree.


00:17:07.896 --> 00:17:09.326
Come on.


00:17:09.361 --> 00:17:11.196
She talks to air more
than she talks to me.


00:17:11.231 --> 00:17:12.664
I could drop dead tomorrow,


00:17:12.699 --> 00:17:14.783
and she'd be too busy
drawing to even notice.


00:17:15.576 --> 00:17:19.205
You know, pictures hold
tremendous power for children.


00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:21.172
Before we learn to speak,


00:17:21.207 --> 00:17:23.730
images are the most
important tool we have


00:17:23.765 --> 00:17:26.594
for understanding the world around us.


00:17:26.629 --> 00:17:29.388
What's real, what matters to us most.


00:17:29.423 --> 00:17:32.302
These are things children
learn to communicate


00:17:32.337 --> 00:17:34.529
almost exclusively through pictures.


00:17:34.564 --> 00:17:36.687
Yeah, her pictures mean something.


00:17:36.722 --> 00:17:40.143
And who is at the center
of nine out of ten of them?


00:17:41.686 --> 00:17:42.944
- Me. -
Mm-hmm.


00:17:42.979 --> 00:17:46.023
Like it or not, you're her world.


00:17:46.058 --> 00:17:49.033
But what if it's not up to me?


00:17:49.068 --> 00:17:50.702
My aunt, she's an
idiot, but she's right.


00:17:50.737 --> 00:17:53.782
No judge in their right mind
is ever gonna side with me.


00:17:53.817 --> 00:17:56.241
