00:28:53.226 --> 00:28:56.568
If there was something to
find, she would have found it.


00:28:56.603 --> 00:28:57.994
Now pay up.


00:28:58.029 --> 00:29:00.407
Uh, I'm sorry? You said 200.


00:29:00.442 --> 00:29:02.122
We had a deal.


00:29:02.157 --> 00:29:04.597
Yeah, that you were gonna find me


00:29:04.632 --> 00:29:07.002
hard proof of criminal endangerment.


00:29:07.037 --> 00:29:10.040
Instead, you've told me
what a nice kid my niece is


00:29:10.075 --> 00:29:12.043
and that my nephew sleeps a lot.


00:29:12.078 --> 00:29:14.354
He really does, though.


00:29:14.389 --> 00:29:16.631
Sleeping is not a crime.


00:29:16.666 --> 00:29:18.181
Is that guy okay?


00:29:18.216 --> 00:29:21.302
I just realized I shouldn't
be hearing any of this.


00:29:21.337 --> 00:29:24.389
As a matter of fact, I
shouldn't be here at all.


00:29:24.424 --> 00:29:25.889
Sit down, Doug.


00:29:27.017 --> 00:29:28.565
So, I guess we're finished here,


00:29:28.600 --> 00:29:31.229
unless either one of
you has a brilliant idea,


00:29:31.264 --> 00:29:33.648
which I realize is highly unlikely.


00:29:33.683 --> 00:29:35.567
Why don't we just kill him?


00:29:38.778 --> 00:29:41.245
Tempting. But no.


00:29:41.280 --> 00:29:44.582
- What else?
- Mike was saying that...


00:29:44.617 --> 00:29:48.954
he really needs this new job
to, like, look good on paper


00:29:48.989 --> 00:29:51.131
for the judge or something.


00:29:51.166 --> 00:29:52.709
Well, that's all very
fascinating, honey,


00:29:52.744 --> 00:29:54.960
but I am not hearing a plan.


00:29:55.836 --> 00:29:57.504
We toss the place.


00:29:58.340 --> 00:30:01.050
Go on.
- Well, he's a security guard, right?


00:30:01.085 --> 00:30:03.927
His job is to make sure nobody gets in.


00:30:03.962 --> 00:30:07.146
So, we get in,


00:30:07.181 --> 00:30:09.106
and we mess up the place good.


00:30:09.141 --> 00:30:11.603
We help ourselves to whatever
we find along the way.


00:30:11.638 --> 00:30:13.444
Your nephew gets canned.


00:30:13.479 --> 00:30:16.774
Judge gives you the
kid, and you give us...


00:30:16.809 --> 00:30:19.360
$2,000.


00:30:20.362 --> 00:30:22.113
One thousand.


00:30:22.905 --> 00:30:26.034
But do it fast, and don't mess it up.


00:30:26.069 --> 00:30:28.324
I mean, you know, mess it up,


00:30:28.359 --> 00:30:30.580
but don't... don't mess this up.


00:30:37.544 --> 00:30:40.095
Come on.


00:30:40.130 --> 00:30:42.132
What are you doing?


00:30:46.053 --> 00:30:47.395
Abby, do you need something?


00:30:47.430 --> 00:30:49.140
No.
- All right, quit playing and take that off.


00:30:49.175 --> 00:30:50.273
I have to go to work.


00:30:50.308 --> 00:30:52.018
I know. I'm coming with you.


00:30:52.053 --> 00:30:53.150
No, you're not.


00:30:53.185 --> 00:30:55.145
- Give me the vest.
- No.


00:30:55.180 --> 00:30:57.894
Give me the vest now.


00:30:57.929 --> 00:31:00.574
I'm coming with you.


00:31:00.609 --> 00:31:02.744
I want to go with you. Abby.


00:31:02.779 --> 00:31:04.613
I don't want to stay here with Max.
- Abby, stop.


00:31:04.648 --> 00:31:06.448
- Hello? -Abby, stop.
- No! You can't make me.


00:31:06.483 --> 00:31:07.758
Yes, I can.
- No, it's mine.


00:31:07.793 --> 00:31:08.999
Hello?


00:31:09.034 --> 00:31:10.794
Let go!


00:31:10.829 --> 00:31:12.789
Let go. No, no. Abby, stop. Abby.


00:31:12.824 --> 00:31:14.787
- He's taking my vest!
- Abby.


00:31:14.822 --> 00:31:16.751
I'm keeping it.
- No.


00:31:19.920 --> 00:31:21.839
She's all yours.


00:32:23.151 --> 00:32:25.070
Garrett!


00:32:32.994 --> 00:32:34.210
Wait, please.


00:32:34.245 --> 00:32:37.546
Please don't-don't... don't run.


00:32:37.581 --> 00:32:40.710
Okay? I-I just want
to know what you saw.


00:32:45.381 --> 00:32:48.468
Please. I'm begging you.


00:32:48.503 --> 00:32:50.302
Help me.


00:32:54.848 --> 00:32:56.601
Who took Garrett?!


00:33:27.257 --> 00:33:29.634
♪ The secrets that you
just can't hide... ♪


00:33:32.720 --> 00:33:35.180
♪ You tell me that you want me... ♪


00:34:10.674 --> 00:34:12.016
About time.


00:34:12.051 --> 00:34:15.679
Starting to think maybe
you fell asleep on the job.


00:34:15.714 --> 00:34:16.854
Um...


00:34:16.889 --> 00:34:19.495
Can I, uh, help you, Officer?


00:34:19.530 --> 00:34:22.102
Please, my name's Vanessa.


00:34:22.137 --> 00:34:24.646
And you must be?


00:34:24.681 --> 00:34:26.531
Um...


00:34:26.566 --> 00:34:29.276
- The new security guard.
- Yeah.


00:34:30.861 --> 00:34:33.197
You're bleeding, by the way.


00:34:36.116 --> 00:34:38.501
Looks nasty.


00:34:38.536 --> 00:34:42.165
Come on. I know where they
keep the first aid kit.


00:34:52.634 --> 00:34:55.178
Love what you've done with the place.


00:34:55.213 --> 00:34:57.097
Why Nebraska?


00:34:57.847 --> 00:35:00.684
- Oh, you need a hand?
- I'm fine.


00:35:01.809 --> 00:35:03.039
You sure?


00:35:03.074 --> 00:35:04.235
Here.


00:35:04.270 --> 00:35:06.070
I'm a certified EMT.


00:35:06.105 --> 00:35:09.692
So if your heart ever goes out,
I'm the one you want to call.


00:35:11.985 --> 00:35:14.072
You seem to really know
your way around the place.


00:35:14.107 --> 00:35:16.299
Well, Freddy's is on my beat.


00:35:16.334 --> 00:35:18.492
I like to stay well-informed.


00:35:20.286 --> 00:35:23.330
Also, I really loved
this place as a kid.


00:35:26.710 --> 00:35:28.133
There.


00:35:28.168 --> 00:35:30.504
That should do it.


00:35:31.380 --> 00:35:33.340
Vanessa Shelly.


00:35:34.175 --> 00:35:35.558
Mike.


00:35:35.593 --> 00:35:37.846
Pleasure to meet you, Mike.


00:35:43.935 --> 00:35:46.855
You doing all right this evening, Mike?


00:35:48.565 --> 00:35:49.613
What?


00:35:49.648 --> 00:35:51.295
Are you good? Are you okay?


00:35:51.330 --> 00:35:52.908
Is everything copacetic?


00:35:52.943 --> 00:35:55.911
Yeah, I know what "all right" means.


00:35:55.946 --> 00:35:57.531
Do you also know that
your eyes are bloodshot


00:35:57.566 --> 00:35:59.446
and your heart rate's through the roof?


00:35:59.481 --> 00:36:01.238
And aside from that gash on your arm,


00:36:01.273 --> 00:36:02.960
which... let's be honest,


00:36:02.995 --> 00:36:06.124
is pretty frickin' bizarre,
you've been acting suspicious


00:36:06.159 --> 00:36:07.875
since the moment you opened the door.


00:36:09.918 --> 00:36:13.673
Yeah, look, it's been a weird night.


00:36:18.052 --> 00:36:20.513
Sounds like Freddy's.


00:36:24.059 --> 00:36:26.227
This place, it gets to people.


00:36:26.978 --> 00:36:29.104
It's one of the reasons
why you're gonna quit.


00:36:29.139 --> 00:36:30.560
I'm sorry?


00:36:30.595 --> 00:36:31.947
Oh, yeah.


00:36:31.982 --> 00:36:34.902
You security hires, you never last.


00:36:38.572 --> 00:36:40.449
Have you met them yet?


00:36:42.076 --> 00:36:43.452
Met who?


00:36:49.249 --> 00:36:51.670
So, what are the other reasons?


00:36:51.705 --> 00:36:52.718
Huh?


00:36:52.753 --> 00:36:54.214
Why you think I'm gonna quit my job.


00:36:54.249 --> 00:36:55.471
Well, you tell me.


00:36:55.506 --> 00:36:57.550
Is this somewhere you see yourself


00:36:57.585 --> 00:36:59.600
ten, 20 years from now?


00:36:59.635 --> 00:37:02.221
I mean, what do I know?
Maybe the benefits are great.


00:37:02.256 --> 00:37:04.897
I didn't think so.


00:37:04.932 --> 00:37:07.936
Add to that the thing with
those kids going missing.


00:37:10.104 --> 00:37:11.529
Wh-What did you just say?


00:37:11.564 --> 00:37:14.109
Prepare to have your mind blown.


00:37:30.458 --> 00:37:32.543
♪ When you close your eyes ♪


00:37:32.578 --> 00:37:33.884
♪ And you go to sleep ♪


00:37:33.919 --> 00:37:35.714
♪ Sleep, sleep, sleep ♪


00:37:37.257 --> 00:37:40.593
♪ And it's down to the
sound of a heartbeat ♪


00:37:40.628 --> 00:37:42.643
This... this is...


00:37:42.678 --> 00:37:45.063
The best thing you've
seen in your entire life?


00:37:45.098 --> 00:37:48.517
♪ I can hear the things
that you're dreaming about ♪


00:37:48.552 --> 00:37:50.519
♪ About, about, about ♪


00:37:52.313 --> 00:37:54.774
- ♪ When you open up your... ♪
- Want to dance?


00:38:04.659 --> 00:38:06.494
Maybe some other time.


00:38:08.662 --> 00:38:12.291
Wait, y-you said some
kids went missing?


00:38:12.326 --> 00:38:14.123
Sure. Back in the '80s.


00:38:14.158 --> 00:38:15.920
What happened to them?


00:38:15.955 --> 00:38:18.263
It was big news.


00:38:18.298 --> 00:38:20.508
That's why the place shut down.


00:38:21.300 --> 00:38:22.641
Wow.


00:38:22.676 --> 00:38:24.721
You really didn't do
your homework, did you?


00:38:25.637 --> 00:38:29.017
And you're not even wearing your badge.


00:38:30.352 --> 00:38:32.562
Got it.


00:38:38.735 --> 00:38:40.076
There.


00:38:40.111 --> 00:38:42.655
Now you're official.


00:38:48.369 --> 00:38:50.462
Hey.


00:38:50.497 --> 00:38:51.796
Some friendly advice?


00:38:51.831 --> 00:38:54.382
Don't let this place get to you.


00:38:54.417 --> 00:38:57.045
Just do your job, and you'll be fine.


00:39:00.464 --> 00:39:02.049
Yeah, sounds good.


00:39:25.031 --> 00:39:26.998
JEFF It's showtime.


00:39:27.033 --> 00:39:30.661
As soon as he gets back, get
the guys and meet me here.


00:39:30.696 --> 00:39:34.082
I think I see a way in.


00:39:47.261 --> 00:39:49.437
All right.


00:39:49.472 --> 00:39:51.786
Now, be quick but thorough.


00:39:51.821 --> 00:39:54.101
Maximum damage, minimum time.


00:39:55.937 --> 00:39:57.814
You see anything valuable, grab it,


00:39:57.849 --> 00:39:59.899
and we'll, uh, settle up after.


00:39:59.934 --> 00:40:01.751
- Good?
- Yeah. Golden.


00:40:01.786 --> 00:40:03.534
- Whoo!
- Yeah!


00:40:03.569 --> 00:40:05.113
- Let's go, boys!
- Come on!


00:41:55.432 --> 00:41:56.725
Carl?


00:42:20.832 --> 00:42:22.125
Hank?


00:42:23.084 --> 00:42:25.461
What the hell are you doing?


00:42:34.011 --> 00:42:36.228
Hank?


00:42:36.263 --> 00:42:37.514
- Hank!
- Jeff?


00:42:39.726 --> 00:42:40.977
Jeff!


00:42:43.521 --> 00:42:44.646
Come on, you stupid...


00:42:44.681 --> 00:42:45.939
Hank?


00:42:47.024 --> 00:42:49.276
Come on. Come on.


00:43:12.258 --> 00:43:13.717
Hank?


00:44:03.059 --> 00:44:04.810
Shit.


00:44:10.817 --> 00:44:14.194
No! No! No!


00:45:15.756 --> 00:45:17.758
Jeff?


00:45:19.469 --> 00:45:20.678
Carl?


00:45:27.602 --> 00:45:28.818
Hey.


00:45:28.853 --> 00:45:30.605
Follow me.


00:45:30.640 --> 00:45:32.781
Hey!


00:45:32.816 --> 00:45:34.504
Hey, wait!


00:45:34.539 --> 00:45:36.193
Come on.


00:45:39.113 --> 00:45:40.781
Hello?


00:45:45.411 --> 00:45:47.789
This way.


00:46:15.483 --> 00:46:17.360
Warmer.


00:46:21.573 --> 00:46:24.992
How in the heck?


00:46:29.997 --> 00:46:32.000
Warmer.


00:47:03.323 --> 00:47:06.658
NARRATOR It's feeding
time for the giraffe.


00:47:13.957 --> 00:47:16.460
Hey, Abs, what you working on?


00:47:19.755 --> 00:47:21.013
All right.


00:47:21.048 --> 00:47:23.885
I guess you don't want this, then.


00:47:28.973 --> 00:47:30.892
It's cool, huh?


00:47:35.938 --> 00:47:38.066
Okay.


00:47:44.280 --> 00:47:46.365
I'm trying my best, Abby, okay?


00:48:06.177 --> 00:48:07.721
Can't you read?


00:48:07.756 --> 00:48:10.264
You okay?


00:48:11.557 --> 00:48:13.621
I made a mess.


00:48:13.656 --> 00:48:15.686
I'm sorry.


00:48:16.604 --> 00:48:19.190
They're just... they're
just papers, all right?


00:48:19.225 --> 00:48:21.109
They don't... they don't mean anything.


00:48:21.144 --> 00:48:23.200
Then why do you have them?


00:48:23.235 --> 00:48:26.031
Well, that's complicated. Aunt Jane...


00:48:26.066 --> 00:48:27.371
I hate her.


00:48:27.406 --> 00:48:29.742
She's mean and she
smells like cigarettes.


00:48:31.453 --> 00:48:32.960
It's not funny.


00:48:32.995 --> 00:48:35.247
You're right, it's not. It's just, uh...


00:48:35.282 --> 00:48:36.839
I don't know, it's nice that


00:48:36.874 --> 00:48:39.439
we can finally agree about something.


00:48:39.474 --> 00:48:41.970
Are you gonna give me away?


00:48:42.005 --> 00:48:44.298
Abs, no, I...


00:48:49.178 --> 00:48:50.658
Hey. Vanessa.


00:48:50.693 --> 00:48:52.355
Hey, Mike.


00:48:52.390 --> 00:48:53.982
And hello.


00:48:54.017 --> 00:48:56.685
Vanessa, this is Abby. Abby, Vanessa.


00:48:56.720 --> 00:48:59.154
Hi, Abby.


00:48:59.189 --> 00:49:01.378
Mike didn't tell me he had a daughter.


00:49:01.413 --> 00:49:03.532
- Gross.
- No, uh, Abby's my sister.


00:49:03.567 --> 00:49:06.904
Ah. Well, he didn't tell
me he had a sister either.


00:49:06.939 --> 00:49:09.413
Are you here to arrest Mike?


00:49:09.448 --> 00:49:11.700
Okay, uh, can you go play in your room


00:49:11.735 --> 00:49:13.744
so me and Vanessa can talk?


00:49:13.779 --> 00:49:15.163
It's nice to meet you.


00:49:16.997 --> 00:49:19.979
What, um... what are you doing here?


00:49:20.014 --> 00:49:22.962
- Somebody broke into Freddy's.
- What?


00:49:22.997 --> 00:49:24.881
Wh-What-what
happened?


00:49:24.916 --> 00:49:27.258
Recognize these?


00:49:28.676 --> 00:49:30.490
Look, it's not what you think, okay?


00:49:30.525 --> 00:49:32.270
Th-Those are... They're sleeping pills.


00:49:32.305 --> 00:49:34.015
- They help me sleep.
- I know what they are, Mike.


00:49:34.050 --> 00:49:35.350
It's written on the bottle.


00:49:36.685 --> 00:49:38.436
News flash: If you're too whacked out


00:49:38.471 --> 00:49:40.188
to remember to lock a friggin' door,


00:49:40.223 --> 00:49:42.228
accident or not, you're liable.


00:49:42.263 --> 00:49:44.458
It's called criminal negligence.


00:49:44.493 --> 00:49:46.653
You wouldn't understand.


00:49:46.688 --> 00:49:48.160
Well, then help me.


00:49:48.195 --> 00:49:50.240
'Cause the moment I file that report,


00:49:50.275 --> 00:49:53.033
it's out of my hands.


00:49:57.037 --> 00:49:59.374
You want to take a walk?


00:50:03.044 --> 00:50:05.754
So I used to have a brother.


00:50:08.007 --> 00:50:10.050
His name was Garrett.


00:50:11.386 --> 00:50:13.846
And when I was...


00:50:13.881 --> 00:50:16.314
about 12,


00:50:16.349 --> 00:50:18.767
he was, uh, he was taken.


00:50:20.144 --> 00:50:22.480
And I was there when it happened.


00:50:24.314 --> 00:50:26.026
They never found the guy who did it,


00:50:26.061 --> 00:50:27.652
and they never found my brother.


00:50:32.866 --> 00:50:36.431
So there's this theory that,
uh, we can't forget things.


00:50:36.466 --> 00:50:39.628
Basically, it says that every
single thing that you see


00:50:39.663 --> 00:50:42.791
in your entire life, down
to the tiniest of details,


00:50:42.826 --> 00:50:44.676
gets stored inside of you.


00:50:44.711 --> 00:50:48.047
You just have to know how to look.


00:50:48.082 --> 00:50:50.181
Your brother...


00:50:50.216 --> 00:50:52.343
You think you saw who took him?


00:50:52.378 --> 00:50:54.311
I know I did.


00:50:54.346 --> 00:50:56.847
And I know that he's in
here, but he's just... he's...


00:50:56.882 --> 00:50:58.023
It's buried.


00:50:58.058 --> 00:51:00.024
So every night, I dream,


00:51:00.059 --> 00:51:01.477
and I go back to that same memory,


00:51:01.512 --> 00:51:03.694
and I-I search for details.


00:51:03.729 --> 00:51:06.648
For any little thing
that got overlooked.


00:51:12.488 --> 00:51:13.996
Yeah.


00:51:14.031 --> 00:51:16.576
And that's usually the part
where people tell me I'm crazy.


00:51:18.745 --> 00:51:20.789
I know what crazy looks like, Mike.


00:51:20.824 --> 00:51:22.808
This isn't it.


00:51:22.843 --> 00:51:24.792
Not even close.


00:51:25.793 --> 00:51:28.303
And these?


00:51:28.338 --> 00:51:30.381
I mean, going back to the same dream,


00:51:30.416 --> 00:51:32.755
the same place night after night,


00:51:32.790 --> 00:51:35.095
it's not easy, so the-the pills help.


00:51:35.130 --> 00:51:36.311
Some other things,


00:51:36.346 --> 00:51:38.263
like familiar sights, familiar sounds.


00:51:38.298 --> 00:51:39.933
"Pining for fun?"


00:51:41.475 --> 00:51:43.860
"Visit Nebraska."


00:51:43.895 --> 00:51:46.446
Your sister seems cool.


00:51:46.481 --> 00:51:49.025
So it's just the two of you?


00:51:49.060 --> 00:51:50.866
Yeah.


00:51:50.901 --> 00:51:53.410
Yeah, it's just us.


00:51:53.445 --> 00:51:56.616
Our mom died a little while back.


00:51:57.700 --> 00:52:01.328
And Dad, he couldn't handle it, so...


00:52:03.164 --> 00:52:04.546
You know what's crazy is, uh,


00:52:04.581 --> 00:52:06.938
when... when Garrett and I were kids,


00:52:06.973 --> 00:52:09.295
they were like those perfect parents


00:52:09.330 --> 00:52:11.338
you'd see on old TV shows.


00:52:13.007 --> 00:52:16.301
Yeah, ev-every night, we
would sit down together,


00:52:16.336 --> 00:52:17.810
we'd have family dinner,


00:52:17.845 --> 00:52:20.640
and we'd hold hands
and say grace, and...


00:52:21.599 --> 00:52:23.357
That actually sounds really nice.


00:52:23.392 --> 00:52:28.355
Yeah, at the time, I
thought it was really cheesy.


00:52:31.026 --> 00:52:32.943
But then it's gone.


00:52:36.573 --> 00:52:40.951
You and Abby, you still have each other.


00:52:42.454 --> 00:52:45.622
From where I sit, I'd say you're lucky.


00:52:50.502 --> 00:52:52.839
I should go.


00:52:56.967 --> 00:52:59.436
No more sleeping on the job.


00:52:59.471 --> 00:53:02.349
When you're at Freddy's, you stay alert.


00:53:05.602 --> 00:53:06.984
<i>MAX Hey, it's Max.</i>


00:53:07.019 --> 00:53:10.148
<i>Leave a message. Or don't.</i>


00:53:13.942 --> 00:53:16.236
Come on, Max. Come on.


00:53:17.738 --> 00:53:20.241
MAX Hey, it's Max. Leave a mes...


00:53:30.167 --> 00:53:31.635
<i>I will work,</i>


00:53:31.670 --> 00:53:33.588
and you will sleep, and
under no circumstances


00:53:33.623 --> 00:53:35.211
are you gonna come out of my office.


00:53:35.246 --> 00:53:36.765
- Do you understand?
- I understand.


00:53:36.800 --> 00:53:40.136
This is not a vacation, okay?
You're not here to have fun.


00:53:40.171 --> 00:53:41.686
Okay.


00:53:41.721 --> 00:53:43.764
Whoa, slow down, slow down, slow down.
- No, no, no.


00:53:43.799 --> 00:53:44.933
Abby?


00:53:51.021 --> 00:53:52.905
Whoa.


00:53:52.940 --> 00:53:55.943
What happened?


00:53:58.195 --> 00:53:59.863
Give me your hand.


00:53:59.898 --> 00:54:01.115
Watch out.


00:54:02.991 --> 00:54:06.036
Do you want me to turn the light off?


00:54:07.955 --> 00:54:09.254
Okay.


00:54:09.289 --> 00:54:11.292
Good night.


00:54:12.543 --> 00:54:14.461
It's like camping.


00:56:12.913 --> 00:56:14.749
BOY Abby?


00:56:30.097 --> 00:56:32.559
I'll be right back.


00:56:45.529 --> 00:56:47.824
Hello?


00:56:53.121 --> 00:56:55.435
I know you're back there.


00:56:55.470 --> 00:56:57.750
Might as well come out.


00:57:25.653 --> 00:57:27.906
You're those kids, right?


00:57:32.160 --> 00:57:34.536
The ones who disappeared?


00:57:38.667 --> 00:57:40.919
Look.


00:57:42.670 --> 00:57:47.257
I don't know how it's
possible that you're here


00:57:47.292 --> 00:57:49.678
like this in my dream, but...


00:57:52.389 --> 00:57:54.181
...I need your help.


00:57:54.216 --> 00:57:56.058
Please.


00:57:57.726 --> 00:58:00.270
Help me remember the
man who took my brother.


00:58:04.858 --> 00:58:07.285
If we show you,


00:58:07.320 --> 00:58:09.196
what will you give us?


00:58:10.198 --> 00:58:11.915
Anything.


00:58:11.950 --> 00:58:14.202
I'll give you anything you want.


00:58:34.179 --> 00:58:35.932
Abby?


00:58:39.018 --> 00:58:41.645
Stop! Stop! Stop!


00:58:41.680 --> 00:58:43.230
Abby?


00:58:54.826 --> 00:58:56.411
Mike.


00:58:58.121 --> 00:58:59.830
They wouldn't stop tickling me.


00:58:59.865 --> 00:59:01.880
I thought I was gonna die.


00:59:01.915 --> 00:59:05.711
Freddy, this is my brother, Mike.


00:59:08.798 --> 00:59:10.695
Abby, what is this? Come on.


00:59:10.730 --> 00:59:12.593
I want you to meet the others.


00:59:24.605 --> 00:59:26.899
Mike, this is Bonnie,


00:59:26.934 --> 00:59:30.278
Foxy and Chica.


00:59:30.313 --> 00:59:32.256
Everyone,


00:59:32.291 --> 00:59:34.199
this is Mike.


00:59:38.870 --> 00:59:40.502
This-this is a joke, right?


00:59:40.537 --> 00:59:42.880
I mean, th-there's someone here.


00:59:42.915 --> 00:59:45.709
There's probably somebody
controlling them, right?


00:59:45.744 --> 00:59:47.169
I mean...


00:59:49.464 --> 00:59:51.389
Okay, good joke!


00:59:51.424 --> 00:59:53.510
Congratulations! You got me!


00:59:53.545 --> 00:59:55.637
You can come out now!


00:59:58.306 --> 00:59:59.641
Hello?


01:00:05.772 --> 01:00:07.322
It's okay, Mike.


01:00:07.357 --> 01:00:09.274
They just want to play.


01:00:12.111 --> 01:00:14.906
We have to go home now. Come on.
- Hold on.


01:00:18.659 --> 01:00:21.121
They really like pictures.


01:00:33.590 --> 01:00:36.197
I had a lot of fun tonight.


01:00:36.232 --> 01:00:39.165
Thank you for playing with me.


01:00:39.200 --> 01:00:42.099
Okay, okay, Abby, come on.


01:00:42.134 --> 01:00:43.976
Okay.


01:00:53.737 --> 01:00:55.821
Bye!


01:01:17.093 --> 01:01:18.720
There you go.


01:01:53.505 --> 01:01:55.757
It's them.


01:02:13.899 --> 01:02:15.367
Hey, Abby, um,


01:02:15.402 --> 01:02:19.154
we need to talk about last night, okay?


01:02:21.199 --> 01:02:22.784
Um...


01:02:23.992 --> 01:02:26.912
So those, uh, those... machines...


01:02:26.947 --> 01:02:29.641
My friends?


01:02:29.676 --> 01:02:32.335
Your friends?


01:02:32.370 --> 01:02:34.385
Um...


01:02:34.420 --> 01:02:36.256
are they...?


01:02:36.291 --> 01:02:38.473
Ghosts?


01:02:38.508 --> 01:02:41.101
- Yeah.
- Of course.


01:02:41.136 --> 01:02:44.055
How else could they
make the robots move?


01:02:46.515 --> 01:02:48.566
Right.


01:02:48.601 --> 01:02:50.310
Can I have some more soup?


01:02:52.021 --> 01:02:53.313
Yeah, sure.


01:02:57.860 --> 01:02:59.988
Hey, Abs.


01:03:00.989 --> 01:03:03.450
You know we used to
have a brother, right?


01:03:04.658 --> 01:03:06.368
Garrett.


01:03:08.579 --> 01:03:11.958
I don't... I don't really
talk about him very much.


01:03:11.993 --> 01:03:14.540
Neither did Mom or Dad.


01:03:14.575 --> 01:03:17.087
Yeah, it was hard for them.


01:03:17.122 --> 01:03:20.007
It's hard for me, too.


01:03:32.269 --> 01:03:35.148
C
- Can you explain this to me?


01:03:36.523 --> 01:03:39.027
You-you drew that, right?


01:03:41.487 --> 01:03:44.491
Okay, and... and-and
you know what that is?


01:03:47.618 --> 01:03:48.917
Hey, hey, it's okay.


01:03:48.952 --> 01:03:50.558
Okay, I'm not, I'm not mad.


01:03:50.593 --> 01:03:52.129
I won't get angry at you.


01:03:52.164 --> 01:03:55.293
But I really need you to
help me understand, please.


01:03:57.837 --> 01:04:00.882
That's when Garrett got taken.


01:04:01.674 --> 01:04:05.260
Abby, who told you about that?


01:04:06.512 --> 01:04:09.557
W- Was it a-a boy
with blonde hair?


01:04:11.392 --> 01:04:14.896
Did that boy ever tell you anything


01:04:14.931 --> 01:04:17.482
about the man driving that car?


01:04:17.517 --> 01:04:18.990
Anything at all?


01:04:19.025 --> 01:04:21.443
Okay, just think,
think really hard, okay?


01:04:26.825 --> 01:04:28.118
No.


01:04:29.618 --> 01:04:32.538
All they talk about is a yellow rabbit.


01:04:33.789 --> 01:04:35.583
Okay.


01:04:36.918 --> 01:04:38.481
But...


01:04:38.516 --> 01:04:40.045
I can ask.


01:04:41.464 --> 01:04:43.924
I would really appreciate that.


01:05:09.784 --> 01:05:17.082
♪ We love the yellow rabbit ♪


01:05:26.216 --> 01:05:27.843
Vanessa's here.


01:05:27.878 --> 01:05:29.143
Yeah.


01:05:29.178 --> 01:05:31.743
My friends talk about her sometimes.


01:05:31.778 --> 01:05:34.274
- What do they say?
- That she's nice.


01:05:34.309 --> 01:05:36.977
Abby, if I asked you to
wait in the car, would you?


01:05:37.012 --> 01:05:38.562
No.


01:05:39.522 --> 01:05:40.780
Abby, wait.


01:05:40.815 --> 01:05:42.282
Guys, I'm back.
- Abby.


01:05:42.317 --> 01:05:45.110
Hey, Vanessa. Abby.


01:05:47.280 --> 01:05:50.372
- Mike.
- Vanessa.


01:05:50.407 --> 01:05:53.577
I missed you guys.


01:05:55.162 --> 01:05:56.998
You knew about this.


01:06:00.417 --> 01:06:01.675
Guess you figured it out.


01:06:01.710 --> 01:06:04.963
Ghost children possessing giant robots?


01:06:04.998 --> 01:06:06.965
Thanks for the heads-up.


01:06:07.000 --> 01:06:09.052
Guys, we need help.


01:06:12.347 --> 01:06:14.021
It needs to be big


01:06:14.056 --> 01:06:16.350
so we can all fit inside.


01:06:20.688 --> 01:06:22.821
Abby, look.


01:06:22.856 --> 01:06:25.283
Now, this is all
really fun and exciting,


01:06:25.318 --> 01:06:27.570
but these things are big,
and they could be dangerous,


01:06:27.605 --> 01:06:29.823
so I think we need to lay
some ground rules, all right?


01:06:29.858 --> 01:06:31.908
Vanessa, what do you think?


01:06:32.991 --> 01:06:36.329
I think we could use
the tables for the fort.


01:06:36.364 --> 01:06:38.974
Everyone, follow me.


01:06:39.009 --> 01:06:41.584
Come on.


01:06:52.136 --> 01:06:54.061
♪ Riding on any wave ♪


01:06:54.096 --> 01:06:55.806
♪ That is the luck you crave ♪


01:06:55.841 --> 01:06:57.617
♪ They don't believe it now ♪


01:06:57.652 --> 01:06:59.393
♪ They just think it's stupid ♪


01:06:59.428 --> 01:07:01.820
♪ So got anything? ♪


01:07:01.855 --> 01:07:03.904
♪ Anyone could have done ♪


01:07:03.939 --> 01:07:05.066
♪ Who would've cared at all... ♪


01:07:05.101 --> 01:07:07.065
It needs to be higher.


01:07:07.100 --> 01:07:09.294
♪ I don't understand ♪


01:07:09.329 --> 01:07:11.055
♪ How a heart is a spade ♪


01:07:11.090 --> 01:07:12.781
♪ But somehow the vital ♪


01:07:12.816 --> 01:07:14.207
You did it!


01:07:14.242 --> 01:07:16.035
♪ Connection is made... ♪


01:07:17.578 --> 01:07:19.872
Are you okay?


01:07:23.125 --> 01:07:25.711
I like it in here.


01:07:25.746 --> 01:07:28.262
Me, too.


01:07:28.297 --> 01:07:31.343
But I think it's gonna rain soon.


01:07:33.428 --> 01:07:35.909
Sounds like we need a roof.


01:07:35.944 --> 01:07:38.390
I'll go see what I can find.


01:07:40.351 --> 01:07:42.644
I'll, uh... I'll-I'll come with you.


01:07:43.937 --> 01:07:46.190
Abby, don't forget to ask.


01:07:46.225 --> 01:07:48.068
- Okay.
- Yeah.


01:07:50.069 --> 01:07:52.071
What are you looking for exactly?


01:07:52.106 --> 01:07:53.830
Tablecloths.


01:07:53.865 --> 01:07:56.658
They used to keep 'em
back here for big events.


01:07:56.693 --> 01:07:59.746
Right. And remind me how you know that.


01:08:02.790 --> 01:08:04.124
Found 'em.


01:08:15.387 --> 01:08:16.393
Don't.


01:08:16.428 --> 01:08:18.075
I wouldn't do that.


01:08:18.110 --> 01:08:19.688
They're spring locks.


01:08:19.723 --> 01:08:21.732
They're on all the older models.


01:08:21.767 --> 01:08:23.651
They were designed to
keep the animatronic parts


01:08:23.686 --> 01:08:27.649
in place so that, uh, a person
could safely wear the suit.


01:08:27.684 --> 01:08:30.694
They tend to be pretty unstable.


01:08:30.729 --> 01:08:31.819
Let's see.


01:08:33.153 --> 01:08:34.572
Ooh.


01:08:36.241 --> 01:08:39.326
Like I said, unstable.


01:08:42.287 --> 01:08:44.958
Is there anything else that you
want to tell me about, Vanessa?


01:08:44.993 --> 01:08:48.085
'Cause you seem to know
everything about this place.


01:08:48.120 --> 01:08:49.374
And what if Abby'd come in here?


01:08:49.409 --> 01:08:50.594
What if she'd found that thing?


01:08:50.629 --> 01:08:53.466
You're the one who
brought her, Mike, not me.


01:08:53.501 --> 01:08:56.510
What I can't wrap my head around is why.


01:08:59.347 --> 01:09:01.481
All right, look.


01:09:01.516 --> 01:09:04.853
I think that they know
who took my little brother.


01:09:05.686 --> 01:09:07.814
I can't explain it, but when I'm here,


01:09:07.849 --> 01:09:09.238
I feel closer to Garrett.


01:09:09.273 --> 01:09:10.816
My dreams are more vivid, and it...


01:09:10.851 --> 01:09:12.857
it's like I can almost...


01:09:12.892 --> 01:09:14.863
Change what happened?


01:09:21.201 --> 01:09:23.038
Did you ask them about this?


01:09:23.073 --> 01:09:24.420
Yeah, I tried.


01:09:24.455 --> 01:09:27.708
I don't think they like me very much.


01:09:28.751 --> 01:09:30.211
But...


01:09:31.295 --> 01:09:33.637
...they do like Abby.


01:09:33.672 --> 01:09:36.975
Mike, you need to drop this.


01:09:37.010 --> 01:09:38.886
I don't really see how
that's any of your business.


01:09:38.921 --> 01:09:41.890
I'm telling you, you need to let it go.


01:09:42.891 --> 01:09:45.268
Who the hell are you?


01:09:46.436 --> 01:09:48.986
Just someone who's trying to help.


01:09:49.021 --> 01:09:51.358
♪ Well, I'm just out of school ♪


01:09:51.393 --> 01:09:53.002
♪ Like I'm real, real cool ♪


01:09:53.037 --> 01:09:54.576
♪ Got to dance like a fool ♪


01:09:54.611 --> 01:09:58.531
♪ Got the message that
I got to be a wild one ♪


01:09:58.566 --> 01:10:01.700
♪ Ooh, yeah, I'm a wild one ♪


01:10:01.735 --> 01:10:03.001
Vanessa, wait.


01:10:03.036 --> 01:10:04.683
♪ Gonna break it loose... ♪


01:10:04.718 --> 01:10:06.331
- Talk to me.
- I'm trying.


01:10:06.366 --> 01:10:07.630
You're not listening.


01:10:07.665 --> 01:10:09.375
Please. Finding the guy that did this


01:10:09.410 --> 01:10:11.085
is the only thing that matters to me.


01:10:15.173 --> 01:10:16.221
Abby?


01:10:16.256 --> 01:10:18.677
Wait. Abby, don't!


01:10:25.517 --> 01:10:27.914
MIKE Abby?


01:10:27.949 --> 01:10:30.312
Abby? Abby!


01:10:34.943 --> 01:10:38.112
What happened? It's okay, Abby.


01:10:38.147 --> 01:10:40.072
You just had an accident.


01:10:40.107 --> 01:10:42.409
You're okay.


01:10:45.202 --> 01:10:47.330
I'm so sorry.


01:10:51.626 --> 01:10:54.420
I don't know what to say.


01:10:54.455 --> 01:10:57.012
Just go home, Mike.


01:10:57.047 --> 01:10:58.632
Take care of your sister.


01:11:00.427 --> 01:11:02.971
What are you so afraid of?


01:11:04.305 --> 01:11:06.647
In the storage room...


01:11:06.682 --> 01:11:09.477
I saw your eyes. You were terrified.


01:11:15.274 --> 01:11:17.443
You can do whatever you
want with your own life,


01:11:17.478 --> 01:11:20.029
but if you ever bring
Abby back here again,


01:11:20.064 --> 01:11:22.322
I will shoot you.


01:11:31.666 --> 01:11:34.091
She looked so angry.


01:11:34.126 --> 01:11:37.963
Why does everyone always
look at you that way?


01:11:57.692 --> 01:12:00.006
Hey, it's Mike.


01:12:00.041 --> 01:12:02.321
I need your help.


01:12:14.334 --> 01:12:15.960
Abby.


01:12:16.920 --> 01:12:18.677
Is that bacon?


01:12:18.712 --> 01:12:20.110
Hey, why don't you, uh, get dressed


01:12:20.145 --> 01:12:21.555
and then come to the kitchen, okay?


01:12:21.590 --> 01:12:22.966
I want to talk to you about something.


01:12:23.001 --> 01:12:24.636
Okay.


01:12:29.765 --> 01:12:33.060
Wow, there's my favorite little girl.


01:12:34.603 --> 01:12:36.398
Come have a seat, all right?


01:12:37.189 --> 01:12:38.822
What did you do?


01:12:38.857 --> 01:12:40.652
Abby, look, I think
if you just sit down,


01:12:40.687 --> 01:12:42.862
we can explain it to you, okay?


01:12:42.897 --> 01:12:44.162
No.


01:12:44.197 --> 01:12:46.615
I promise you, this is
not what you think it is.


01:12:46.650 --> 01:12:49.334
I hate you.


01:12:49.369 --> 01:12:51.578
I hate you, Mike!


01:12:54.916 --> 01:12:57.836
Well, I-I think that went well.


01:13:10.681 --> 01:13:12.683
She reminds me of you, you know.


01:13:12.718 --> 01:13:15.360
Always with the temper.


01:13:15.395 --> 01:13:16.652
Well, look, when she calms down,


01:13:16.687 --> 01:13:18.481
can you, um, tell her that I'm sorry


01:13:18.516 --> 01:13:21.115
and that I'll-I'll be back soon?


01:13:21.150 --> 01:13:25.196
Well, Mike, there's
a larger conversation


01:13:25.231 --> 01:13:27.080
that needs to happen here.


01:13:27.115 --> 01:13:29.492
So when you do get back,
you and me are gonna have


01:13:29.527 --> 01:13:31.161
a little chat.


01:13:31.196 --> 01:13:33.121
Okay.


01:13:39.294 --> 01:13:42.130
♪ Celebrate good times, come on ♪


01:13:44.923 --> 01:13:46.890
♪ Let's celebrate ♪


01:13:46.925 --> 01:13:48.969
♪ Celebrate good times... ♪


01:13:49.004 --> 01:13:50.979
You know what works for me?


01:13:51.014 --> 01:13:54.058
A warm glass of milk
with chamomile and honey.


01:13:54.093 --> 01:13:55.934
I tell you...


01:13:58.438 --> 01:14:00.648
What an asshole.


01:14:54.952 --> 01:14:56.849
Okay, enough games, you two.


01:14:56.884 --> 01:14:58.733
Emergency landing.


01:14:58.768 --> 01:15:00.548
Coming in.


01:15:00.583 --> 01:15:02.751
Hey, buddy.


01:15:03.837 --> 01:15:05.463
Well, don't just stand there. Dig in.


01:15:10.969 --> 01:15:12.971
Sweetheart, what's wrong?


01:15:13.930 --> 01:15:16.689
This... this isn't...


01:15:16.724 --> 01:15:19.018
this isn't how it happened.


01:15:20.061 --> 01:15:21.485
This isn't real.


01:15:21.520 --> 01:15:23.023
But it could be.


01:15:24.315 --> 01:15:26.824
What is this?


01:15:26.859 --> 01:15:28.528
This isn't what I asked for.


01:15:28.563 --> 01:15:30.787
But it's what you want.


01:15:30.822 --> 01:15:34.366
No. I just, I just want
to find the man that...


01:15:34.401 --> 01:15:35.667
You're lying.


01:15:35.702 --> 01:15:37.669
You want to save Garrett.


01:15:37.704 --> 01:15:39.664
That's why you're really here.


01:15:39.699 --> 01:15:42.166
To change what happened.


01:15:42.201 --> 01:15:43.977
To go back.


01:15:44.012 --> 01:15:45.753
But I can't.


01:15:46.962 --> 01:15:48.589
He's gone. They're all gone.


01:15:48.624 --> 01:15:50.759
Really?


01:15:58.808 --> 01:16:01.727
You can have this dream every night.


01:16:01.762 --> 01:16:04.646
You can be together with him again.


01:16:04.681 --> 01:16:07.232
Like before.


01:16:07.267 --> 01:16:08.950
How?


01:16:08.985 --> 01:16:12.614
You said we could have
anything we wanted.


01:16:13.405 --> 01:16:17.284
We want Abby.


01:16:19.454 --> 01:16:21.331
Abby?


01:16:25.000 --> 01:16:29.172
They love her, Mike, and she loves them.


01:16:31.132 --> 01:16:33.655
You've seen her with them.


01:16:33.690 --> 01:16:36.178
You've seen how happy she is.


01:16:38.890 --> 01:16:42.232
It's time to let her go, sweetheart.


01:16:42.267 --> 01:16:46.147
You were never the right
person to take care of her.


01:16:58.325 --> 01:17:00.953
Okay.


01:17:04.832 --> 01:17:06.918
Yes.


01:17:11.672 --> 01:17:13.758
You're home.


01:17:28.814 --> 01:17:31.026
No.


01:17:32.735 --> 01:17:34.326
No, this is wrong.


01:17:34.361 --> 01:17:37.198
I don't, I don't want this. Listen...


01:17:49.794 --> 01:17:52.011
I made a mistake!


01:17:52.046 --> 01:17:54.590
Please, I don't want this!


01:17:54.625 --> 01:17:56.301
Do you hear me?!


01:17:59.679 --> 01:18:01.639
You leave Abby alone!


01:18:06.643 --> 01:18:08.485
KIDS Abby.


01:18:08.520 --> 01:18:10.071
Abby.


01:18:10.106 --> 01:18:12.441
Stay away from my sister!


01:18:16.779 --> 01:18:18.405
Abby.


01:18:19.824 --> 01:18:21.867
- Abby.
- Abby.


01:18:26.121 --> 01:18:27.831
Abby.


01:18:30.960 --> 01:18:33.629
KIDS Abby. Abby.


01:18:33.664 --> 01:18:36.298
Abby. Abby. Abby.


01:18:40.094 --> 01:18:42.305
BOY Abby.


01:19:54.836 --> 01:19:57.505
No!


01:20:04.094 --> 01:20:06.271
Abby?


01:20:06.306 --> 01:20:09.350
You can't stay in
there forever, you know.


01:20:14.397 --> 01:20:15.898
Suit yourself.


01:20:25.200 --> 01:20:26.658
ANNOUNCER The pottery that grows.


01:20:26.693 --> 01:20:28.043
It's easy.


01:20:28.078 --> 01:20:29.870
Soak your Chia overnight,
spread the seeds...


01:20:31.163 --> 01:20:33.415
Oh.


